  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "DCOUNTA counts non-blank matching cells (or records when field is omitted), requires 2+ rows in database/criteria, and rejects non-reference databases at entry (0x800A03EC)",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, DCOUNTA(database, [field], criteria) counts every non-blank cell (numbers, text, logicals, errors) in the chosen field column across matching records (or counts matching records when field is omitted), matches un-operatored text criteria as case-insensitive prefixes, requires both database and criteria to be ranges with at least one record row below headers (#VALUE! otherwise), and rejects literal numbers or array constants in database at formula entry (COM 0x800A03EC). All 5,676 full-bank DCOUNTA rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence admit3-answers-dcounta-range-mixed.json, DnaCalc prefix_metadata row 266, and crates/calc-fml/tests/fixtures/entry/excel-entry.tsv; 5,676/5,676 full-bank rows match.",
